# Backend CI/CD (NestJS sales API)

The API is a **separate** Hostinger Cloud Startup **Node.js Web App** + dedicated MySQL. Never run Nest on the static SPA instance (`noexec` / esbuild). See `docs/deployment/hostinger-api.md`.

**Do not use a VPS.** Stay on Cloud Startup. Prisma uses a JS MariaDB driver adapter so the native query engine is not required at runtime. Apply schema SQL in phpMyAdmin; do not run `prisma migrate deploy` on the host.

## Split

- **Local:** `pnpm dev:api` against `apps/api/docker-compose.yml` MySQL.
- **CI:** `.github/workflows/api.yml` on `migration/backend-api` — `prisma generate` + `nest build` on `ubuntu-latest`, then commit `apps/api/dist`.
- **CD:** Hostinger Node app (`lime-chamois-337700.hostingersite.com`), Framework **Other**, empty build, **start / entry** `start-api.mjs` (or `dist/main.js`). Env: `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `CORS_ORIGIN`, `UPLOAD_DIR`.

`UPLOAD_DIR` must sit **outside** the git checkout (redeploys wipe `apps/api`). PDFs are not committed. Never `prisma seed` / `migrate deploy` on Hostinger.

`apps/api` `postinstall` runs `prisma generate --schema=./prisma/schema.prisma` so Hostinger’s monorepo `pnpm install` still generates the client (adapter is JS-only). That is allowed; compiling Nest on the host is not.

## Do not

- Deploy this API on the Vite/SPA Web App.
- Run `vite build` or `nest build` on the host.
- Flip production `VITE_API_MODE=api` until `GET /api/health` and `GET /api/health/db` succeed.
- Move the API to a VPS.
- Leave Hostinger **entry/start** empty — without `start-api.mjs` or `dist/main.js` the site returns Hostinger’s 404 HTML.

SPA publish stays `.cursor/rules/frontend-cicd.mdc`.
